<title>GREECE: Greek Alpha Credit, IFC, EBRD to launch fund.</title>
<headline>Greek Alpha Credit, IFC, EBRD to launch fund.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dunabe Fund, founded by Greece's Alpha Credit Bank group in cooperation with the IFC and the EBRD, will be launched on Wednesday, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>The initial capital is $15.6 million and the goal is to raise the amount to $25-$30 million, the fund said.</p>
<p>Dunabe Fund has already opened offices in Athens and Bucharest and will participate in the share capital of new private firms active in the Balkans and especially Romania, it said.</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
